 ### [Volume Bounds Computation](5114-volume-bounds-computation.md)
-Volume Bounds Computation computes an Axis-Aligned Bounding Box (AABB) that encloses a set of 3D points, optionally applying padding to ensure the volume fully contains the geometry with a safety margin. It serves as the foundational step for initializing voxel grids, spatial indices, and rendering volumes in implicit and explicit volume rendering pipelines. Unlike [Mesh Bounding Box Calculation](3612-mesh-bounding-box-calculation.md), which operates on mesh vertices, this method generalizes to any point cloud or sampled data structure. It differs from [Silhouette-based Bounding Box Initialization](5448-silhouette-based-bounding-box-initialization.md) by requiring explicit 3D coordinates rather than inferring bounds from 2D projections [G].
