 ### [Host-side Bounding Box Computation](13468-host-side-bounding-box-computation.md)
-Host-side Bounding Box Computation computes the axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) for each triangle in a mesh on the CPU host, producing separate arrays for minimum and maximum coordinates. It serves as the prerequisite step for GPU-based voxelization by providing the spatial extent of each primitive before ray-primitive intersection or volume rasterization [G]. It differs from [Mesh Bounding Box Calculation](3612-mesh-bounding-box-calculation.md), which computes a single global AABB for the entire mesh, by maintaining per-triangle bounds.
